# Phase 5 STOP-LATE-EVENT: a turn held mid-stream (working), stopped with
# Ctrl-C and a second prompt typed in the same read as the stop, so the
# prompt is in hand before the stopped turn has ended. xfx's runtime then
# sends the stopped turn's end and the prompt's start with no wait between,
# and the UI reads them in one drain: the prompt's working must still
# follow a frame that shows its Thinking. Then done, and the exit clears
# the record.
gateway p5-lifecycle-osc-interruptnext-turns.json
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 4
type first question
key Enter
held
wire s00-working
key C-c s e c o n d Space q u e s t i o n Enter
release
held
wire s01-second
release
wait 2
wire s02-done
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 2
wire s03-exit
